= Choosing our enemies

In our media and campaign materials, who should we consider as our main opponents?

[? if enemies != 0 : Previously, we had considered the [+ enemies +] as our prior enemies. Is a change of direction necessary? ?]

- @spd: The so-called "social-facists" - the SPD.
- @far_right: The far right - the NSDAP and DNVP.
- @nsdap: The NSDAP alone.
- @right_wing: Every party to the right of the SPD.
- @pro_republic: The Weimar Coalition parties - the SPD, Z, and DDP.
- @bourgeois: The bourgeois parties - the Center and DVP.
- @easy_discard

@pro_republic
on-arrival: enemies = "pro republic"; ultra-left_strength += 5; stalinist_strength += 5; conciliator_dissent += 5; right_dissent += 5; workers_spd -= 3; workers_z -= 1; spd_relation -= 10; ddp_relation -= 10; z_relation -= 10

Attacking the pro-republican parties is popular among all but the Conciliators and the Right wing of our party, who would prefer to be fighting the far-right parties. This might also hamper our ability to reconcile with the SPD in the future.

@far_right
on-arrival: enemies = "far right"; workers_nsdap -= 3; workers_dnvp -= 3; right_strength += 5

Attacking the far right is popular among the entire party, although many consider the bourgeois parties to be just as dangerous. 

@right_wing
on-arrival: enemies = "right wing"; dvp_relation -= 5; z_relation -= 5; workers_z -= 2; workers_nsdap -= 2; workers_dnvp -= 2

Attacking the Right is popular among the entire Left.

@nsdap
on-arrival: enemies = "NSDAP"; nazi_urgency += 1; workers_nsdap -= 4

[? if nazi_urgency == 0 or nsdap_r < 10 : The NSDAP is a tiny party right now, with more bark than bite. Many in our party are questioning our choices. ?][? if nazi_urgency > 0 and nsdap_r >= 10 : The Nazis are the most urgent problem for us to deal with. ?]

@spd
on-arrival: enemies = "SPD"; stalinist_strength += 5; right_dissent += 8; conciliator_dissent += 5; spd_relation -= 15; workers_spd -= 4

Attacking the SPD is supported by the Ultra-Left and Stalinists, but not the Conciliators and Right. However, if we are to reconcile with the SPD, this may not be the best choice.

@bourgeois
on-arrival: enemies = "bourgeois parties"; dvp_relation -= 5; z_relation -= 5; workers_z -= 3

Our anti-bourgeois rhetoric is popular among the whole party, and does not surprise anyone.
